------------------------------------------------------------------------
In fulfillment of the requirement from section 2.4.6 of the Academic
Regulations in Princeton's Rights, Rules, Responsibilities guide,
and the COS 217 Generative AI policy, disclose and describe how you
used AI in completing this assignment:


Megan- 
I used ChatGBT for help understanding assignement specifications, I throughrly read through the assignment instrustions and would ask ChatGBT if I was confused with a prompt but just used to understand not to write any code.
I used ChatGBT for help better understanding C concepts like typedef and ->. I read through the textbook as well to understand but just wanted to solidify understanding with more interpretations.
William and I wrote our functions together but I still went back and tried to reproduce functions on my own and asked ChatGBT if I did things correctly and to explain previous logic we had to current logic. 
I used ChatGBT to help me debug CritTer priority messages and to check to make sure my comments were good, I still tried to debug myself first and all comments were my own thinking and writing. 
I used ChatGBT to walk me through how to use Valgrind but also went through the precept guide to learn better. 
I used ChatGBT because I was not pushing and pull properly from github so asked ChatGBT what I was doing wrong.
I used AI to check my logic for the Makefile and if I had my dependencies right. I also used ChatGBT to help me find a syntax error in my Makefile that I could not find for some reason. 

William and I- 
We had a memory leak we could not identify so we used AI to help identify were our memory leak was and then suggestion on how to fix it. It told us that we should swap pointers of hashtables when expanding our hashtable so we implemented this suggestion writing our own code to do so. 

